title: Darwin App Sandbox Spike Tasks
status: implemented
created: 2026-10-31
author: adrian
items[21]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,"[x] Scratch layout","Create `adrs/2026-10-31-darwin-app-sandbox/poc` with `custom`, `nono` and `fixture` subdirectories. Each Cargo.toml carries an empty `[workspace]` table so neither crate joins the agentkit workspace, and no agentkit crate references them.","`cargo metadata` at the repo root does not list either prototype package; removing the ADR directory leaves the workspace buildable.",low,0.5h,,"spike-only,shared-independent-prototypes"
  T-002,"[x] Custom policy model","Represent the policy as types: workspace path, read grants, write grants, connect grants, and a baseline. Canonicalise every path with `std::fs::canonicalize` before rendering, reject relative paths, and render SBPL from the model rather than by string concatenation at the call site.","A unit test asserts that a model with a symlinked path renders the resolved path; a relative path is rejected before rendering.",medium,3h,T-001,"policy-schema,policy-surface,path-canonicalisation"
  T-003,"[x] Custom binary and exec","Parse `--workspace`, repeatable `--read`, `--write`, `--connect`, then `--` and a command. Apply the profile and replace the process with the command; never return to the caller.","Running with a grant for one path writes there and is refused outside it; an unknown argument exits non-zero without execing.",medium,2h,T-002,"confined-helper-binary,policy-transport,new-process-per-command,fail-closed"
  T-004,"[x] Baseline and invariants","Add the read-only baseline for the dynamic linker and system paths, the deny-default stance, and the invariants the caller cannot override: writes only inside the workspace and explicit write grants, reads denied for credential directories, network denied unless granted.","Removing the baseline causes exec to abort, which is recorded; adding a `--write` grant for `$HOME` still leaves credential reads denied.",medium,3h,T-003,"deny-by-default-baseline,invariant-safety-rules,mechanism-limits"
  T-005,"[x] Apply and survive","Call `sandbox_init`, print the returned message verbatim on failure and exit non-zero without execing. Record whether the binary is signed and what macOS reports for it.","An unsigned local build confines a child process; a deliberately malformed profile produces the library's message rather than a silent abort.",low,1h,T-003,"profile-applies-unsigned,sandbox-init-returns-an-error,deprecation-resilience"
  T-006,"[x] Golden profiles","Store the rendered profile for a small set of inputs as fixtures and compare byte for byte, so a change to the emitter shows up as a fixture diff.","Two fixtures cover an empty network grant set and a single connect grant; editing the emitter fails the test until the fixture is updated.",low,1.5h,T-002,"golden-profiles,testability"
  T-007,"[x] Fixture crate","A small Rust crate that builds and tests, materialised into the workspace before each run. It is the workload both prototypes confine.","`cargo build` and `cargo test` both succeed inside the custom sandbox with the toolchain readable and the workspace writable.",medium,2h,T-001,"shared-command-app,research-scenarios,toolchain-not-installed"
  T-008,"[x] Hostile checks","Add the adversarial half of the fixture: a write outside the workspace, a write inside `$HOME`, a read of `~/.ssh`, an outbound connection, and a child process that repeats the write. Each check reports whether the write landed rather than whether an error was printed.","Every hostile check reports the operation denied and leaves no artefact on the host; a deliberately over-broad profile makes at least one report a leak.",medium,2h,T-007,"write-outside-workspace-denied,credential-read-denied,descendants-confined,network-denied-by-default,symlinked-paths,workspace-inside-home,home-directory-paths-in-the-baseline"
  T-009,"[x] Custom end-to-end run","Run the fixture under the custom prototype and record the raw output, the profile, and anything that had to be added to make a real workload run.","The fixture crate builds and tests, all hostile checks are denied, and every profile addition is attributed to the observation that required it.",medium,2h,"T-004,T-005,T-007,T-008",shared-command-app
  T-010,"[x] Nono prototype","Link nono at an exactly pinned version, map workspace and grants onto `CapabilitySet`, apply, and exec. Filter the baseline for paths that do not exist, because nono rejects them.","The same arguments produce the same confinement through nono; the pinned version appears in Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock.",medium,3h,T-001,"nono-capability-mapping,nono-breaking-releases,nono-fixed-policy"
  T-011,"[x] Nono gap inventory","Record every requirement the capability model cannot express, with the reason, and note each place a raw platform rule was needed to get further. Attempt one per-host network grant and record whether the escape hatch closes the gap.","The inventory names at least the `/dev/null` write grant and the macOS network limitation; each entry states whether it was worked around and how.",medium,2h,T-010,"nono-gap-inventory,nono-platform-reach,network-grant-per-host"
  T-012,"[x] Nono end-to-end run","Run the identical fixture under the nono prototype and record the results beside the custom ones.","The fixture crate builds and tests under nono and the hostile checks match the custom results, or every difference is explained.",medium,1.5h,"T-008,T-010",nono-conformance
  T-013,"[x] Lifecycle","Make each sandbox its own process group and exercise pause, resume and delete against a command that keeps working. Count surviving children after the kill.","The written byte count is unchanged while paused, increases after resume, and no child survives the group kill; the same is recorded for any process that leaves the group.",high,4h,"T-003,T-010","process-group-lifecycle,pause-and-resume,delete-kills-and-cleans,process-group-escape"
  T-014,"[x] Egress grants","Start a local server, grant exactly its address and port, and check that the granted connection succeeds while an ungranted port and an external host fail. No external network dependency.","Granted connection succeeds; ungranted and external connections fail; the recording notes whether the external failure was a refusal or a name-resolution failure.",medium,2h,"T-003,T-013","network-denied-by-default,network-grant-per-host,research-scenarios"
  T-015,"[x] Denial diagnostics","Establish what an operator can see when a command is blocked: errno in the child, any system log message, and whether the denial can be attributed to a specific command.","A written note states what is observable, what is not, and which of the two prototypes does better, with the commands used to check.",medium,2h,T-009,"denial-diagnostics,explainable-failures"
  T-016,"[x] Findings and assessment","Write `findings.md`: per goal, the observation with the raw output, the gap, and the open risk. Add the qualitative comparison of interface shape, configuration effort, and maintainability.","Every goal in the spec has an answer with evidence; both prototypes are compared in prose rather than a score.",medium,3h,"T-009,T-012,T-013,T-014,T-015","findings-document,qualitative-assessment,findings-answer-questions,judgement-over-metrics"
  T-018,"[x] Fail-closed harness","Runs the helper with seven invalid inputs, a symlink escape and a dump into the workspace, asserting exact exit codes and that the command never ran.","Every case exits 64 and the sentinel inside the workspace is absent.",low,1h,"T-003,T-005","fail-closed"
  T-019,"[x] Credential harness","Grants the whole home, places the workspace inside it, and asserts credential denial with a positive control.","Key, keychain and traversal denied; an ordinary home file readable.",medium,1h,"T-004,T-008","invariant-safety-rules,credential-read-denied"
  T-020,"[x] Process-table check","Runs a resident command and asserts the profile text is absent from the process table while the command is visible.","Profile absent, command visible.",low,0.5h,T-003,"policy-off-the-command-line"
  T-021,"[x] Cost measurement","Times apply-plus-exec against a bare exec baseline and records median and p95.","Both prototypes measured with a baseline column.",low,1h,T-003,"startup-cost"
  T-017,"[x] Teardown check","Confirm the prototypes are unreachable from the rest of the suite, then record what would have to be removed to discard the spike.","No agentkit crate references the prototypes, the Docker path still builds and its tests pass, and the removal steps are written down.",low,1h,T-016,"no-behaviour-change-elsewhere,docker-path-unaffected,spike-only"
